post_install() {
    udevadm control --reload-rules 2>/dev/null || true
    udevadm trigger --subsystem-match=hidraw 2>/dev/null || true
    cat <<'EOF'

m693ctl installed.

The udev rule tags the mouse's control interface with uaccess, which covers a
normal logged-in desktop session. If you are on a setup where that does not
apply (a remote session, or no logind seat), add yourself to the input group:

    sudo usermod -aG input "$USER"      # then log out and back in

Re-plug the receiver, then check with:  m693ctl list
The graphical tool is m693-gui, and needs the optional pyside6 package.

EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
    udevadm control --reload-rules 2>/dev/null || true
}

post_remove() {
    udevadm control --reload-rules 2>/dev/null || true
}
